From: jackwang0009 <93422958+jackwang0009@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:10:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] [upstream-candidate] Write colors in their own color space

CPDF_PageContentGenerator wrote every non-gray color as DeviceRGB,
dropping the color space (Separation, Lab, ICCBased, Indexed, DeviceN,
Pattern, CalGray/CalRGB) and, for Separation /None, painting a black
block where the original is blank. Write the color in the space it was
set in: device spaces keep g/G, rg/RG, k/K with the raw components;
CalGray/CalRGB/Lab/ICCBased write `/Name cs` + components + `sc`/`SC`;
Separation/DeviceN/Indexed write `/Name cs` + components + `scn`/`SCN`;
patterns write the pattern color space, the underlying color for
uncolored tiling patterns, and `/Name scn`/`SCN`. Resource names are
reused when they still refer to the same space, otherwise the array is
realized as a new FXC resource (FXP for patterns). A color space that
cannot be referred to by name falls back to the equivalent RGB color.

The parser now keeps the resource name that selected a CalGray/CalRGB/
Lab/ICCBased color space instead of clobbering it with the family name,
and threads the pattern resource name through the color state, so the
generator can reuse the names.

Tests: CPDFPageContentGeneratorTest.ProcessColorSpaces covers Lab
(stored name), DeviceCMYK/DeviceGray (raw components) and Separation
/None (written back faithfully).

Verification (ops_diff.py): synthetic colour diffs 259 -> 0, public
1303 -> 0; no-diff pages 38/67 -> 54/67 synthetic, 373/388 -> 384/388
public.
